Temporary Cua Driver 0.34.1 Windows console fix.
Upstream base: trycua/cua@0c69d9a2c8abbb5051a2df4a23f0fa166d5385dc

Apply with git apply in an upstream checkout, then build:
  cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path libs/cua-driver/rust/Cargo.toml -p cua-driver-sdk
  cargo test --locked --release --manifest-path libs/cua-driver/rust/Cargo.toml -p cua-driver-sdk embedded::tests::embedded_child_has_no_console

For a Windows desktop test artifact, set T3CODE_CUA_DRIVER_SDK_LIBRARY to the
absolute path of target/release/cua_driver_sdk.dll under libs/cua-driver/rust,
then run the normal desktop artifact builder. Both the Electron host and
server sidecar receive the override. Build separately for each architecture.
Remove this patch and the packaging override when an upstream release fixes it.

